# Reset state after trst_ni is wrong

This

https://github.com/pulp-platform/riscv-dbg/blob/358f90110220adf7a083f8b65d157e836d706236/src/dmi_jtag_tap.sv#L306

should reset the TAP to the `Test-Logic-Reset` state.

See `4.6.1 Specifications` in `IEEE Standard for Test Access Port and Boundary-Scan Architecture 11491-2013`. @msfschaffner does that sound correct to you too?







PR title: src: Fix wrong reset state for TAP after trst_ni

Source: https://github.com/pulp-platform/riscv-dbg/pull/169

PR description:
The PR addresses a bug where the TAP (Test Access Port) reset state was incorrect after `trst_ni` assertion. According to the author: "This problem was didn't become visible as most/all drivers always run the software reset sequence as trst_ni is an optional signal."

Linked issue:
- #165 "Reset state after trst_ni is wrong"

Activity:
The fix was subsequently applied upstream by Andreas Kurth in the OpenTitan project (July 15, 2024), which also reverted two related commits that had replicated the same problem in their DV (design verification) code.

Key details:
- Author: bluewww
- Status: Merged
- Merge date: July 8, 2024
- Commits: 1 commit merged
- Changes: Corrects the reset value of `tap_state_q`
- Impact: Fixes edge cases where `trst_ni` is used without software reset sequences
